  "title": "Consciousness is fundamentally affective",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "c36b9530-0be7-44ac-a467-13517142bed7",
      "text": "If the brainstem consciousness is the primary kind, then consciousness is fundamentally affective. The arousal processes that sustain wakefulness are not a mere quantitative level of consciousness but carry qualitative content of their own: it feels like something to be awake, and those qualia are affects.",
